# Decouple Admin Panel to Standalone Application (`apps/admin`)

Isolate the Admin Dashboard and Live Ingestion Console from the public-facing passenger commuter application (`apps/web-app`) into a brand new standalone Next.js project inside `apps/admin`.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Port Configuration**: The new standalone admin application will run on port `3003` in development mode (`npm run dev`), keeping it completely isolated from `web-app` (port `3001`) and `backend` (port `5000`).
> - **Shared Server Compatibility**: The backend CORS config already allows connections from all origins, so the admin page on port `3003` will communicate perfectly with the REST endpoints on port `5000`.

---

## Proposed Changes

### New Standalone Workspace App (`apps/admin`)

#### [NEW] Initialization of `apps/admin` Workspace
- Create the target folder [admin](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin).
- Initialize Next.js project template using:
  `npx -y create-next-app@latest ./ --ts --app --src-dir --eslint --use-npm --disable-git --yes`
- Install [lucide-react](https://npmjs.com/package/lucide-react) icons library in the admin app:
  `npm install lucide-react`

#### [NEW] [page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin/src/app/page.tsx)
- Recreate the Admin Dashboard Monitor as the main root page (`/`) of the new admin app.
- This will render the stats blocks, the retro scrolling terminal log, and the active tracked buses grid on access.

#### [NEW] Port Configuration in `package.json`
- Modify the `dev` script in `apps/admin/package.json` to force Next.js to start on port `3003`:
  `"dev": "next dev -p 3003"`

